===Question #1===
{{Cquote2|Firstly, tell us about yourself! Who are you, and what do you do?}}

* '''Mod Halo:''' Hey, I’m Mod Halo. I’m a Senior QA on the Old School team. I test all the things, and I’ve been at Jagex for just over three years now. Two years of that has been on Old School, so I’m finally making my stream debut - and I’ve been working more recently on the Tombs of Amascut raid!

===Question #2===
{{Cquote2|What is your experience with OSRS?}}

* '''Mod Halo:''' I played Old School since release. I played a bit on and off, quit a few times - but you never really quit Old School; you just take long breaks! My main account is an Ironman account, but I’ve been playing on a Group Ironman account more recently.
* '''Mod Halo:''' It’s quite funny that I test RuneScape all day in my day job, then I go home and play some more RuneScape. It’s great!

===Question #3===
{{Cquote2|What's your most favourite thing about the game? And what's your least favourite thing about the game?}}

* '''Mod Halo:''' One of the big things I love about the game is the community and the players - how passionate they are! For something more game-related, I’d say the different Game Modes we have and how players can play the game differently. Ironman Mode, Group Ironman more recently, even Leagues. Making people think differently about how to play the game. That stuff I absolutely love.
* '''Mod Halo:''' My least favourite isn’t much. If I had to say, it would be the mid-level to low-level guidance for players on what to do. The game is huge, so things like, “What’s my next goal? Should I go for Slayer? Should I go for Fire Cape? Should I go for Quest Cape?”. All that is very open and not really clear for players.
* '''Mod Halo:''' We’ve got the Activity Advisor coming out, which should hopefully solve that, but I think that’s my biggest gripe with the game.

===Question #4===
{{Cquote2|I hear you might be moving away from QA soon?}}

* '''Mod Halo:''' I will! Really exciting news; towards the end of this month, I will be going on a different path from QA. I will be joining the Content Dev team, which is super exciting. I’m just so excited about it, especially with the projects coming up at the end of the year and starting next year.

===Question #5===
{{Cquote2|Lastly, Did you come across any bugs that you caught before ToA’s release?}}

* '''Mod Halo:''' There are a few funny ones. I chatted to Mod Curse because we worked quite closely on this. Because it’s such a large project, there are bound to be a few funny ones. So I’ll go through a list I’ve written - some are pretty funny!
* '''Mod Halo:''' So the first one is one that people might have seen on my Twitter, or Elena’s Twitter, which is the mini-Akkha. Akkha got resized to be tiny, which made it arguably one of the hardest mechanics in the game because you couldn’t click on him.
* '''Mod Halo:''' The next bug, ironically, is also a bug. With Kephri’s slam attack, which she does when making a special attack, she would just do that for the entire fight. She’d just be bobbing up and down the entire thing - that was great!
* '''Mod Halo:''' The last one is quite a weird one. In Akkha’s boss room, there’s an invocation that puts orbs in front and behind you. If you go to the edge of the arena, since it’s a circle, if you go to the edge and you try to put an orb in a place that isn’t part of the map, since there’s nothing down there in the shadow area, it would default to an NPC, and that NPC was the Tool Leprechaun! So now and then, you’d see a Tool Leprechaun appear at the edge of Akkha’s arena.
* '''Mod Halo:''' I’ll never forget the day that Curse sent a screenshot of it in our chat, and we said, “that’s not real!”. But it was, and it was hilarious.

==ToA General Questions==
===Question #1===
{{Cquote2|How has the release been for everyone so far?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=95t7YVRRkGo&t=550s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Halo:''' I think the release has been really good. There’s been a few bumps in the road recently, but overall it’s just been such a fantastic experience. The launch especially, because lots of us came into the office, and it’s been a long time since we’ve seen everyone together. We’ve got the TVs on and streams of people completing the raid. It was just awesome.
* '''Mod Kieren:''' Oh, what a launch! It’s been incredible. Genuinely, it was an amazing day for us internally as well. We had our little celebrations on Zoom, and we also did a little get-together in the office. It’s been fantastic. We had the CEO come in to congratulate us and everything! That was great.
* '''Mod Kieren:''' For the launch, watching it live with a group of us in the office, we had TV screens up watching it. The reception has blown all of us away of how loved the raid was right from the start! We wanted it to be accessible with the entry mode aspect, but we also wanted to let people put it to the limit with invocations.
* '''Mod Kieren:''' I’m really happy with how invocations have been received too. I was talking about it week after week on this Q&A stream about how incredible the art and animations are. The death animation for the final boss is insane! It’s incredible.
* '''Mod Kieren:''' I remember working on Verzik for Theatre of Blood and being blown away that she turned into a bat and flew up into the sky. That was pretty cool. This is another level! People don’t like how long it is because they failed the time challenge, and I think we’re tweaking that.
* '''Mod Kieren:''' Incredible raid, incredible reception. As Halo says, there’s been a few bumps in the road and a few kinks we’re working out, but overall I’m over the moon with how this has gone. It’s a testament to everyone who’s worked on the project.
* '''Mod Light:''' If you like the art, we’re planning an art-dedicated stream sometime this week if all goes well. Hopefully, you’ll find out more about the art of ToA in that dedicated stream.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I think the release went well. I’ve been working on it for almost a year now, and when you’ve been staring at the same project day in, day out, you start to go a little bit insane and think, “I don’t know if this is actually good. It’s kind of cool but will it actually live up? Will it be fun after the first completion?”.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' The success has been outstanding, and there’s a lot of reassurance there that people seem to enjoy it. People seem to still enjoy it even after 100 clears, which is what I was really worried about. It’s gone really well.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I know the first week, I was stalking every stream I could, trying to fix all the bugs and fix any balance issues. We had a huge patch last week; there was loads of feedback about bugs to fix and things too hard that needed to be changed. There were certain phases and mechanics that people were just skipping, and I think the biggest offender there was Wardens P2. You didn’t need to coordinate at all; you could just skip that entire phase. Four Twisted Bow hits, and the boss goes down.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' There was a certain pride in me as a developer, thinking, “they’re just skipping the entire boss; it’s boring”. I was looking to fix that because I wanted people to engage in the content, but there are also balance reasons. This was supposed to be the supply sink in the raid, and people just skipped the supply sinks.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' I also thought from a balance perspective; it did need to be a little harder. We can see what happened there. We double-down on changes, triple-down on changes, and whilst all the individual ones looked okay, we released a massive patch that made the raid significantly harder - much harder than we had anticipated.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' Friday last week was stressful, trying to get a hotfix together that addressed all these changes and then QA them properly because we didn’t want to rush them out before a weekend and break the raid right before the weekend, as well as communicating the entire process to you.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' There was this whole sentiment of, “oh, you’re just basing it around a couple of Twitch streamers and content creators saying it’s too easy, " which wasn’t the case at all. There were so many facets of feedback coming in. We were taking it all in, looking at data and playing it ourselves. We really wanted to get rid of that stigma in a comprehensive, communicative blog, which I think went down well on Friday, and I think the rates are really nice now.

===Question #2===
{{Cquote2|Are you happy with the outcome now?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=95t7YVRRkGo&t=866s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' For the most part, I’m pleased with where the raids are currently playing at. There are still a few bugs and things to fix that would be nice QoL, such as a Quick Entry on all the doors, barriers and crystals, just to smooth out that experience. We’ve still got a couple of weeks scheduled where we can tidy things up.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' We don’t want it to be where we just delegate all these fixes to months or years in the future; we want to get the raid into a good spot. Things will turn up over time, but all of the significant issues like the Quick Pass - which I think is a legitimate thing where there’s dialogue box after dialogue box when you’re trying to go as fast as possible. You want to get rid of all those annoyances.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' This week is also a bit of an invocation balance pass. We didn’t do that last week, but we wanted just to review all of the invocations, change a couple of values and make some higher or lower. For any of the specific invocations that were badly balanced, we want to change them up since some aren’t really doing anything at all, and some are doing way too much.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' An excellent example of that is path levelling. Path levelling seems a big mechanic of the raid that everyone is skipping. We tried to emphasise that by rewarding a bunch of raid levels, but people are just opting out.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' We’re looking at a couple of things in terms of the stats that is added for levelling.  We’re also looking at some mechanics that maybe shouldn’t level up and just be static. Hopefully, this will make that more of an enticing tradeoff where you’re getting a good amount of raid level and loot potential versus the difficulty increase. So we’ll see how that feels.
* '''Mod Light:''' More information will be in this week’s news post. Just a reminder about the game update this week. It’s on Thursday to allow us some time to test all the changes that we’ve made.

===Question #3===
{{Cquote2|We’ve passed 1.5 million completions of ToA. Did you think the uptake would be this massive?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=95t7YVRRkGo&t=997s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Kieren:''' No, is the short answer! I didn’t expect it to hit one and a half million completions already. We hit one million super fast. It’s mind-blowing. It’s been so long since we released a raid, so I think that’s also a factor. There’s a lot of hype and pent-up demand from four years of not adding raids, but it’s also a testament to how well this appeals across entry mode through to expert. It did remarkably well and let some players raid who’d never been able to raid before.
* '''Mod Kieren:''' I didn’t expect it to be this popular! Behind the scenes, we’ve got a lot more data, and it’s been fascinating. I know that Arcane, you’ve been reviewing our different data dashboards. It’s fascinating to see the different size groups that players are doing it with, the completion times, the number of completions, the success rates of raids and which drops are coming into the game. It’s fascinating to look at, and it’s also helping us make some of our tweaks and decisions.
* '''Mod Light:''' Are you noticing a new demographic of players trying raids since we tried this new system?
* '''Mod Kieren:''' From a data side, I don’t think that we’ve gotten quite that deep yet. But looking at the stats of who’s playing it and the combat levels of those people playing it, it certainly feels that way. Many players have dabbled a little bit with Chambers and Theatre of Blood but haven’t really gotten into raiding, and now this is turning into a place where they can go, “Okay, I can get to grips with raiding”. Maybe the next step is to try out Theatre of Blood and get into the other raid content that the game has.

